20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET2     ESMX_Driver: index=  35                         MPIR_CVAR_GPU_COLL_STAGING_BUF_SIZE : This variable determines the size of the staging buffers used for some collectives (such as MPI_Allreduce) when sendbuf/recvbuf on GPU-resident buffers. This variable has no effect if  MPICH_GPU_COLL_STAGING_AREA_OPT is set to 0.   Default: 262144
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET2     ESMX_Driver: index=  36           MPIR_CVAR_GPU_COLL_REGISTER_SMALL_STAGING_BUFFERS : On AMD & NVIDIA GPUs, for small payloads, GPU Memcpy to regular malloc'ed CPU-attached buffers is not expensive as it used to be.  It is actually more expensive to register small CPU-attached memory staging regions for each operation. On the other hand, for large payloads, it is better to register these CPU-attached buffers. Hence, for collective algorithms with log(N) based patterns, (such as recursive-doubling), we skip the registration operation. For algorithms that are used for larger payloads, such as, reduce-scatter-allgather, we register the tmp buffers since experiments suggest that this is helpful.  We don't know what the story will be on Intel GPUs, so we will have to revisit this when we have the right hardware.  Default: 0
