20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  72                            MPIR_CVAR_OFI_CXI_COUNTER_REPORT : Determine if CXI counters are collected during the job, and the verbosity  of the counter data report that is displayed during MPI_Finalize. Recognized values are between 0 and 5. _CTR_REPORT_DISABLE      0 - no CXI counters are collected _CTR_REPORT_DEFAULT      1 - network timeout counters collected, 1-line display _CTR_REPORT_SUMMARY      2 - #1 + CXI counters collected, summary report displayed _CTR_REPORT_ON_ERROR     3 - #2 + displays counter data for nodes that hit a timeout _CTR_REPORT_ALL_ON_ERROR 4 - #2 + displays all node counter data if a timeout occured _CTR_REPORT_ALL          5 - #2 + displays all node counter data
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  73                              MPIR_CVAR_OFI_CXI_COUNTER_FILE : Specifies a file containing an optional list of CXI counter names to collect. If  this file is present, instead of collecting the default set of MPI counters, this  set will be used instead. Counter names need to be listed one per line. The default network timeout counters will be collected in addition to the file contents.
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  74                       MPIR_CVAR_OFI_CXI_COUNTER_REPORT_FILE : Specifies an optional output filename for the counter report. By default, the  counter report is written to stdout. If this env var is specified, the node- specific counter data produced with MPIR_CVAR_OFI_CXI_COUNTER_REPORT options 3,  4 and 5 will be written to node-specific files with filenames of  MPIR_CVAR_OFI_CXI_COUNTER_REPORT_FILE.hostname.   This is useful when running on hundreds or thousands of nodes, where stdout can  get jumbled and/or truncated by the launcher. If not specified, stdout is used.
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  75                           MPIR_CVAR_OFI_CXI_COUNTER_VERBOSE : If set to a non-zero value, this enables more verbose output about the CXI counters collected. Can be helpful for debugging and/or identifying which counters are being collected.
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  76                                    MPIR_CVAR_OFI_HWCOLL_OPT : Specifies the hardware collective policy. Either 0, 1, or a named list 0 = all supported hwcolls are disabled 1 = all supported hwcolls are enabled To enable hwcoll algorithms for selected MPI collectives, set the  value to a comma-separated list of the desired collective names.  Names are not case-sensitive. Any unrecognizable name is flagged  with a warning message and ignored. For example, to enable the  MPI_Barrier and MPI_Allreduce hwcoll algorithms, set  MPICH_OFI_HWCOLL_OPT=mpi_barrier,mpi_allreduce The following collective names are recognized: MPI_Barrier,  MPI_Allreduce, MPI_Bcast Default: Not enabled.
