20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  91                           MPIR_CVAR_OFI_RMA_STARTUP_CONNECT : If set to 1, CrayMPICH RMA will create static OFI connections to every other rank on the same node during MPI_Init. This will also enable MPIR_CVAR_OFI_STARTUP_CONNECT.
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  92                                MPIR_CVAR_OFI_DEFAULT_TCLASS : If set, CrayMPICH will assign the requested default TC (traffic class) to the job domain.  By default, all endpoints inherit this TC.
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  93                                 MPIR_CVAR_OFI_TCLASS_ERRORS : Determines how CrayMPICH responds to traffic class errors.  Valid values are "warn", "silent" or "error".
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  94                                  MPIR_CVAR_OFI_CXI_PID_BASE : Set to the base value that MPI will use to assign portal IDs for the CXI provider.  Max PID value is 510.  MPI uses PID_BASE+lrank as the unique value per rank per node.  This is only applicable to SS11.
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  95                                 MPIR_CVAR_OFI_CXI_VNI_INDEX : If the application launcher gives us more than one CXI VNI, use the VNI at this index in the list. By default the VNI at spot 1 is shared between many job-steps, but cannot be used with Scalable Start up.
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  96                          MPIR_CVAR_OFI_USE_SCALABLE_STARTUP : Disabled by default. This feature requires WLM support, which is only available in PALs, as it was removed from Slurm. We may decide to deprecate this in the future. This is only applicable to SS11.
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  97                            MPIR_CVAR_OFI_RMA_LATENCY_TCLASS : Set this to make small message non-ordered RMA (MPI_Put/MPI_Get) use low latency traffic class.
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  98                  MPIR_CVAR_OFI_RMA_LATENCY_TCLASS_THRESHOLD : This enviroment varible determine the maximum message size of non-ordered RMA operations that will utilize low latency traffic class.
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index=  99                                       MPIR_CVAR_UCX_VERBOSE : If set to 1, enable verbose output about the CH4 UCX device. If set to 2 or higher, enable more verbose output.
20260922 035643.494 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 100                                  MPIR_CVAR_UCX_RC_MAX_RANKS : By default, CrayMPI selects either the UCX RC or UD protocols for inter-node messaging.  If a job is launched with MPICH_UCX_RC_MAX_RANKS  ranks or fewer, the RC protocol is selected.  If more ranks are launched,  the UCX UD protocol is chosen.  The RC protocol does not scale well due to the resource requirements.  Note this default can be overridden by setting the UCX_TLS environment variable.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 101                              MPIR_CVAR_SMP_SINGLE_COPY_MODE : If non-null, choose an on-node copy mode for large messages. This variable can be set to XPMEM, CMA, or NONE. By default, Cray MPICH will look to use XPMEM. If XPMEM is requested, but not available, Cray MPICH will attempt to use CMA. If both XPMEM and CMA cannot be used, Cray MPICH will fall back to using the ANL shared memory implementation (2-copy) Default: NULL
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 102                              MPIR_CVAR_SMP_SINGLE_COPY_SIZE : Specifies the minimum message size in bytes to consider for single-copy transfers for on-node messages. This applies only to the SMP (on-node shared memory) device. The value is interpreted as bytes, unless the string ends in a K, which indicates kilobytes, or M, which indicates megabytes. Default: 1024
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 103                           MPIR_CVAR_XPMEM_COALESCE_ATTACHES : Specifies whether MPICH should size new entries into its XPMEM cache that they fully overlap any prior entries where there was a partial overlap. This will allow MPICH to evict the prior entries. When the kernel has to handle memory map / unmap events in regions where there are multiple overlaping XPMEM attaches, it may lead to poor performance. Default: 0
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 104                       MPIR_CVAR_SHM_PROGRESS_MAX_BATCH_SIZE : Adjusts the maximum number of on-node requests that can be processed in a single batch. Higher values for the maximum batch size can lower the overhead due to entering the progress engine, but can also delay the processing of off-node message requests. Default is 8.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 105                                 MPIR_CVAR_CH4_PROGRESS_POKE : If set to 1, this cvar allows MPI to call progress_test() from within MPID_Isend (ch4_send.h). Progress_test() is called only if GPU support is enabled and if the posted_list is non-NULL. If this is set to 0, progress_test() is skipped. This variable defaults to 1. If GPU support is enabled, we allow MPID_Isend to call progress_test(), if posted_list is non-empty.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 106                          MPIR_CVAR_CH4_OFI_FORCE_AM_ATOMICS : If set to 1, this cvar forces all OFI RMA atomics to use acctive messaging. This variable defaults to 1.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 107                            MPIR_CVAR_CH4_PROGRESS_POKE_FREQ : This cvar controls how often a process calls progress_test() from within MPID_Isend (ch4_send.h). Progress_test() is called only if GPU support is enabled and if the posted_list is non-NULL.  This variable is not relevant if MPICH_CH4_PROGRESS_POKE is 0.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 108                                MPIR_CVAR_CH4_RMA_THREAD_HOT : If true, the big lock is disabled for certain RMA operations
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 109                                    MPIR_CVAR_ABORT_ON_ERROR : If set, causes MPICH to abort and produce a core dump when MPICH detects an internal error. Note that the core dump size limit (usually 0 bytes by default) must be reset to an appropriate value in order to enable coredumps. Default: Not enabled.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 110                                   MPIR_CVAR_CPUMASK_DISPLAY : If set, causes each MPI rank in the job to display its CPU affinity bitmask. Note that this reports only the CPU affinity masks for the MPI ranks; if you have a hybrid program, it does not provide any thread information. The bitmask is read from right to left, meaning the value in the rightmost position corresponds to CPU 0 on the node.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 111                                       MPIR_CVAR_ENV_DISPLAY : If set, causes rank 0 to display all MPICH environment variables and their current settings at MPI initialization time. Default: Not enabled.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 112                                  MPIR_CVAR_OPTIMIZED_MEMCPY : Specifies which version of memcpy to use. Valid values are: 0         Use the system (glibc) version of memcpy. 1         Use an optimized version of memcpy if one is available for the processor being used. In this release, an optimized version of memcpy() is available only for Intel processors. 2         Use a highly optimized version of memcpy that provides better performance in some areas but may have performance regressions in other areas, if one is available for the processor being used. In this release, a highly optimized version of memcpy() is available only for Intel Haswell processors. Default: 1
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 113                              MPIR_CVAR_OPTIMIZED_MEMCPY_MAX : If an optimized version of memcpy is used for copying data between buffers, instead of the system (glibc) version, then it will not be used for copies larger than this value. The version of memcpy used is controlled by the MPICH_OPTIMIZED_MEMCPY environment variable. Default: 511
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 114                                     MPIR_CVAR_STATS_DISPLAY : If set to 1, a summary of MPI statistics, also available through the MPI Tools Interface, will be written by rank 0 to stderr. If set to 2, all ranks will produce an individualized statistics summary and write to file on a per-rank basis. The MPICH_STATS_FILE determines the prefix of the file to be used. This information may provide insight into how MPI performance may be improved. Default: 0
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 115                                   MPIR_CVAR_STATS_VERBOSITY : Specifies the verbosity of the MPI statistics summary. This information may provide insight into how MPI performance may be improved. Increase the value for more detailed summary. Default: 1 1        USER_BASIC  (default) 2        USER_DETAIL 3        USER_ALL 4        TUNER_BASIC 5        TUNER_DETAIL 6        TUNER_ALL 7        MPIDEV_BASIC 8        MPIDEV_DETAIL 9        MPIDEV_ALL
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 116                                        MPIR_CVAR_STATS_FILE : Specifies the filename prefix for the set of data files written when MPICH_STATS_DISPLAY is set to 2. The filename prefix may be a full absolute pathname or a relative pathname. Default: _cray_stats_
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 117                              MPIR_CVAR_RANK_REORDER_DISPLAY : If set, causes rank 0 to display which node each MPI rank resides in. The rank order can be manipulated via the MPICH_RANK_REORDER_METHOD environment variable or MPIR_CVAR_RANK_REORDER_METHOD control variable. Default: Not set
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 118                               MPIR_CVAR_RANK_REORDER_METHOD : Overrides the default MPI rank placement scheme. If this variable is not set, the default aprun launcher placement policy is used. The default policy for aprun is SMP-style placement. To display the MPI rank placement information, set MPICH_RANK_REORDER_DISPLAY. See manpage for more details. Default: 1, for SMP-style placement.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 119                               MPIR_CVAR_USE_PERSISTENT_TOPS : If set, causes MPICH to allow using triggered operations for persistent communication operations whenever possible. The availability of the triggered operations depends on the networking HW used, the number of HW counters available for usage and other items. Default: Not enabled
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 120                      MPIR_CVAR_DISABLE_PERSISTENT_RECV_TOPS : If set, will disable the use of the triggered operation for receives. This variable is specifically created to avoid using receive operations with triggered operations on systems that doesn't provide access to HW based triggered receive operations. This variable has no effect, if the MPICH_USE_PERSISTENT_TOPS variable is not set. Default: Not enabled
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 121                                MPIR_CVAR_ENABLE_ACTIVE_WAIT : If set, will enable the use of the active wait semantics. Active wait is the semantics where the wait or waitall operation for a user passed request waits until it becomes active. Meaning, on usage of persistent operations, wait will return immediately if the prequest is not started. Active wait semantics replaces the above MPI semantics and waits on the prequest until it becomes active. This feature is important for GPU Direct Async advanced GPU features like ST and KT, where the HOST process can wait on the request before the GPU Control Processor (ST) or the GPU thread (KT) starts the operation. Setting this env variable will enable active wait support. Default: Enabled
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 122                                 MPIR_CVAR_MAX_TOPS_COUNTERS : Specifies the maximum number of HW counters to be opened for performing the deferred work queues. Triggered operation should be enabled for this variable to take effect. Default: 64
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 123                                   MPIR_CVAR_VERSION_DISPLAY : If set, causes MPICH to display the CRAY MPICH version number as well as build date information. Default: Not enabled
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 124                          MPIR_CVAR_GPU_USE_STREAM_TRIGGERED : If set, causes MPICH to allow using stream triggered GPU communication operations. Default: Not enabled
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 125                 MPIR_CVAR_GPU_DISABLE_STREAM_TRIGGERED_TOPS : If set, causes MPICH to disable using triggered operations with stream triggered GPU communication operations. With the triggered operations disabled all stream triggered operations are enabled using a progress thread. Default: Not enabled
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 126          MPIR_CVAR_GPU_DISABLE_STREAM_TRIGGERED_NIC_OFFLOAD : If set, causes MPICH to disable using NIC offload for triggered operations with stream triggered GPU communication operations. With the NIC offloading disabled, all triggered operations for stream triggered communication if enabled will use the progress thread for communication progress. Default: Not enabled
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 127                          MPIR_CVAR_GPU_USE_KERNEL_TRIGGERED : If set, enables persistent MPI operations to be triggered from a device kernel. Default: not set
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 128               MPIR_CVAR_GPU_USE_STREAM_TRIGGERED_SET_SIGNAL : If set, causes MPICH to allow using stream triggered GPU communication operations with atomic set operations for signaling purpose. Default: Not enabled
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 129               MPIR_CVAR_GPU_USE_STREAM_TRIGGERED_AMO_SIGNAL : If set, causes MPICH to allow using stream triggered GPU communication operations with atomic increment operations for signaling purpose. Default: Not enabled
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 130                                  MPIR_CVAR_MEMCPY_MEM_CHECK : If set, enables a check of the memcpy() source and destination areas. If they overlap, the application asserts with an error message listing the file, line, and memory range overlap. If this error is found, correct it either by changing the memory ranges or possibly by using MPI_IN_PLACE. Default: not set (off)
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 131                                     MPIR_CVAR_MSG_QUEUE_DBG : If set, turns on TotalView Message Queue Debugging support so that message queues are tracked in the TotalView debugger and a message queue graph can be generated. Enabling this feature degrades performance. Default: not enabled.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 132                             MPIR_CVAR_NO_BUFFER_ALIAS_CHECK : If set, the buffer alias error check for collectives is disabled. The MPI standard does not allow aliasing of type OUT or INOUT parameters on the same collective function call. The use of MPI_IN_PLACE is required in these scenarios. A new check was added in MPT 5.2 to detect this condition and report the error. To bypass this check, set MPICH_NO_BUFFER_ALIAS_CHECK to any value. Default: not set
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 133                                MPIR_CVAR_ALLOC_MEM_AFFINITY : Controls the affinity of the memory region allocated by the MPI_Alloc_mem() or MPI_Win_allocate() operations. On systems that do not offer High Bandwidth Memory capabilities, (such as Intel Haswell or Broadwell processors), this env. variable is ignored and memory affinity is set to DDR. On Phi processors, such as KNL (and KNH, KNP in the future), this env. variable allows users to specifically request the memory returned by MPI_Alloc_mem() and MPI_Win_allocate() to be bound to either DDR, or the MCDRAM. Users can request a specific page size or memory binding policy via the MPICH_ALLOC_MEM_POLICY and MPICH_ALLOC_MEM_PG_SZ env. variables. Default: SYS_DEFAULT
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 134                             MPIR_CVAR_INTERNAL_MEM_AFFINITY : Controls the affinity of internal memory regions allocated by the MPI library. This variable currently affects the memory affinity of the mail-boxes used for off-node communication, and the shared-memory regions that are used for on-node pt2pt and collective ops. On systems that do not offer High Bandwidth Memory capabilities, (such as Intel Haswell or Broadwell processors), this env. variable is ignored and memory affinity is set to DDR. On Phi processors, such as KNL (and KNH, KNP in the future), this env. variable allows users to specifically request the internal memory regions used by the MPI library to be bound to either DDR, or the MCDRAM. The default affinity settings will be governed by the system defaults. For example, on a KNL system configured in the Quad/Flat mode, if the job is run with numactl --membind=1, all of MPI's internal memory will be bound to MCDRAM if this variable is not set. Default: SYS_DEFAULT
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 135                                  MPIR_CVAR_ALLOC_MEM_POLICY : Controls the memory affinity policy on systems with specialized memory hardware. By default, the memory policy is set to "{P}referred". Other accepted values are "{M}andatory" and "{I}"nterleave. Default: Preferred
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 136                                   MPIR_CVAR_ALLOC_MEM_PG_SZ : Controls the page size for the MPI_Alloc_mem() and MPI_Win_allocate() operations. This parameters defaults to 4KB base pages. The supported values are 2M, 4M, 8M, 16M, 32M, 64M, 128M, 256M, 512M, 1G and 2G. Default: 4096
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 137                                   MPIR_CVAR_OPT_THREAD_SYNC : Controls the mechanism used to implement thread-synchronization inside the Cray MPICH library. If set to 1, an optimized synchronization implementation is used. If set to 0, Cray MPICH falls back to using a pthread_mutex-based thread-synchronization implementation. Default: 1
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 138                                 MPIR_CVAR_THREAD_YIELD_FREQ : Determines how often a thread yields while waiting to acquire a lock in the new Cray optimized locking impl. This variable has no effect if MPICH_CRAY_OPT_THREAD_SYNC is 0. Default: 10000
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 139                                   MPIR_CVAR_MEM_DEBUG_FNAME : If set, the MPI library creates new files with the user specified name and writes various important memory statistics into these files. This information can be useful for post-processing. Users can set MPICH_MEM_DEBUG_FNAME to any suitable string. The resulting files are named as "string".<pid>.<MPI-rank>. For example, if MPICH_MEM_DEBUG_FNAME is set to "MEM_DBG_MSGS" the debug file for rank0 will be named "MEM_DBG_MSGS.<pid>.0 and written to the user's current working directory. If this flag is not set, the MPI library will redirect all the debug messages to stderr. Default: unset (disabled)
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 140                                   MPIR_CVAR_MALLOC_FALLBACK : Set the policy for fallback behavior when attempting to allocate large pages for internal buffers and insufficient large pages are available to satisfy the request. If set to enabled, MPICH falls back to using malloc in such cases. Default: not enabled (process fails and job terminates if insufficient large pages are available to satisfy the request)
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 141                              MPIR_CVAR_NO_DIRECT_GPU_ACCESS : If true, IPC and NIC-GPU Direct Access capabilities are not used for GPU-to-GPU transfers. This is mainly used for debugging. Default: 0
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 142                                      MPIR_CVAR_G2G_PIPELINE : If nonzero, the device-host and network transfers will be overlapped to pipeline GPU-to-GPU transfers. Setting MPICH_G2G_PIPELINE to N will allow N GPU-to-GPU messages to be efficiently in-flight at any one time. If MPICH_G2G_PIPELINE is nonzero but MPICH_GPU_SUPPORT_ENABLED is disabled, MPICH_G2G_PIPELINE will be turned off. If MPICH_GPU_SUPPORT_ENABLED is enabled but MPICH_G2G_PIPELINE is 0, the default value is set to 8. The pipeline-based implementation is being carried over from CH3/Aries implementation. We think the pipelined-based implementation will not be necessary on SS-11 systems. This logic may get dropped in the future. Default: not set
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 143                               MPIR_CVAR_GPU_SUPPORT_ENABLED : If set, allows the MPI application to pass GPU pointers directly to MPI communication functions. Default: not set
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 144                               MPIR_CVAR_GPU_MAX_NUM_STREAMS : Specifies maximum number of GPU Stream handles a process can use to implement intra-node D2D, D2H, and H2D operations. This is only applicable to systems with  NVIDIA GPUs.  Default: 1
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 145                            MPIR_CVAR_GPU_IPC_CACHE_MAX_SIZE : Specifies maximum number of GPU IPC cache handles a process can retain in its IPC cache at a given point in time.  Default: 50
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 146                MPIR_CVAR_GPU_MANAGED_MEMORY_SUPPORT_ENABLED : If set, allows the MPI application to pass pointers allocated via GPU managed memory allocators to MPI communication functions. Default: set if using NVIDIA GPUs
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 147                         MPIR_CVAR_GPU_COLL_STAGING_AREA_OPT : If set, allows Cray MPI to use pre-registered CPU-attached memory to optimize collective ops. Default: set
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 148               MPIR_CVAR_GPU_COLL_REGISTER_SHARED_MEM_REGION : If set, allows Cray MPI to registere CPU-attached shared memory regions used to optimize collective ops. Default: set
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 149                                   MPIR_CVAR_GPU_IPC_ENABLED : If set to 1, Cray MPICH will use GPU IPC to move data between GPU devices that are within the same node. If set to 0, Cray MPICH will use staging buffers on the host to implement data transfer between GPU devices that are within the same node. If MPIR_CVAR_GPU_SUPPORT_ENABLED is set, Cray MPICH automatically attempts to enable the IPC optimizations. If MPIR_CVAR_NO_DIRECT_GPU_ACCESS is set, IPC optimizations are disabled. Default: -1
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 150                                 MPIR_CVAR_GPU_IPC_THRESHOLD : Specifies the minimum message size in bytes to consider for single-copy transfers between two different GPU devices that are within the same compute node. The value is interpreted as bytes, unless the string ends in a K, which indicates kilobytes, or M, which indicates megabytes.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 151                        MPIR_CVAR_GPU_IPC_INTRAGPU_THRESHOLD : Specifies the minimum message size in bytes to consider for single-copy transfers between two ranks using the same GPU device that are on the same compute node. The value is interpreted as bytes, unless the string ends in a K, which indicates kilobytes, or M, which indicates megabytes.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 152                                  MPIR_CVAR_GPU_IPC_PROTOCOL : Specifies the protocol used for large msg on-node, inter-GPU data transfers via GPU IPC. Valid options are RPUT or RGET. Default: RGET
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 153                                 MPIR_CVAR_GPU_NO_ASYNC_COPY : If set, disables the use of asynchronous memcpy's for on-node GPU-aware transfers. Default: 0
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 154                                      MPIR_CVAR_ENABLE_YAKSA : If set, enables the use of the YAKSA datatype engine for packing and unpacking non-contiguous buffers in both CPU- and GPU-attached memory. Default: 0
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 155                       MPIR_CVAR_GPU_EAGER_REGISTER_HOST_MEM : If set to 1, enables MPI to request POSIX eager memory to be registered with the GPU runtime. This is an optimization to improve the performance of small message intra-node, inter-GPU MPI ops that use POSIX shared memory as bounce buffers. If set to 0, this optimization is disabled and we rely on GTL to lock/unlock host memory regions for a given on-node, small msg inter-GPU transfer. Default: 1
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 156                         MPIR_CVAR_GPU_REDUCTIONS_USE_KERNEL : If set, adds a hint that the use of device kernels for reduction operations is desired.  MPI is not guaranteed to use a device kernel for all reduction operations.  This variable is relevant only if MPICH_GPU_SUPPORT_ENABLED  is set to 1. GPU kernel-based optimizations are currently disabled for Reductions that involve the use of MPI_IN_PLACE and non-contig MPI datatypes. This feature is also used only when user buffers are on GPU-attached memory regions.  This optimization is applicable for MPI_Allreduce, MPI_Reduce, MPI_Reduce_scatter, and MPI_Reduce_Scatter_block. Default: 1
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 157                           MPIR_CVAR_GPU_REDUCTIONS_BLK_SIZE : Controls the size of the GPU-attached staging buffer user for GPU-kernel-based optimizations for MPI_Allreduce, MPI_Reduce, MPI_Reduce_scatter and MPI_Reduce_scatter_block. Defaults to 64MB per process, but increasing this value may improve performance for very large payloads. This variable is relevant only if MPICH_GPU_REDUCTIONS_USE_KERNEL and MPICH_GPU_SUPPORT_ENABLED are also set.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 158                    MPIR_CVAR_GPU_ALLREDUCE_KERNEL_THRESHOLD : MPI_Allreduce collectives with payloads equal to or larger than this threshold can utilize the GPU kernel-based optimization.  The default value for AMD GPUs is 16384. The default for NVIDIA and INTEL GPUs is 131072. This variable is relevant only if MPICH_GPU_REDUCTIONS_USE_KERNEL and MPICH_GPU_SUPPORT_ENABLED are also set.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 159                       MPIR_CVAR_GPU_REDUCE_KERNEL_THRESHOLD : MPI_Reduce collectives with payloads equal to or larger than this threshold can utilize the GPU kernel-based optimization. This variable is relevant only if MPICH_GPU_REDUCTIONS_USE_KERNEL and MPICH_GPU_SUPPORT_ENABLED are also set.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 160               MPIR_CVAR_GPU_REDUCE_SCATTER_KERNEL_THRESHOLD : MPI_Reduce_scatter collectives with payloads equal to or larger than this threshold can utilize the GPU kernel-based optimization. This variable is relevant only if MPICH_GPU_REDUCTIONS_USE_KERNEL and MPICH_GPU_SUPPORT_ENABLED are also set.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 161         MPIR_CVAR_GPU_REDUCE_SCATTER_BLOCK_KERNEL_THRESHOLD : MPI_Reduce_scatter_block collectives with payloads equal to or larger than this threshold can utilize the GPU kernel-based optimization. This variable is relevant only if MPICH_GPU_REDUCTIONS_USE_KERNEL and MPICH_GPU_SUPPORT_ENABLED are also set.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 162                          MPIR_CVAR_GPU_A_A_MEMCPY_THRESHOLD : This is the  message size that and below which cray-mpich will use system memcpy to perform memcpy for AMD GPU-attached buffer instead of GPU-aware memcpy. This is an internal tuning parameter. This variable is relevant only if MPICH_GPU_SUPPORT_ENABLED is set and the application is running on AMD GPU platform.
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 163                                   MPIR_CVAR_RMA_MAX_PENDING : Determines how many RMA operation may be outstanding at any time over libfabrics. RMA operations beyond this max will be queued and only issued as pending operations complete. Default: 64
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 164                                MPIR_CVAR_RMA_SHM_ACCUMULATE : If set to 1, enables SHM accumulate operations. If set to 0, disables SHM accumulate operations. It also sets the default for the window hint "disable_shm_accumulate". Default: 1
20260922 035643.495 INFO             PET3     ESMX_Driver: index= 165                                MPIR_CVAR_LOCAL_SPAWN_SERVER : If set to a non-zero value, lazily sets up a spawn server for single node jobs the first time that MPI_Comm_spawn is called. The variable has no effect for multi-node jobs. If set to a  value greater than 0, the spawn server will use this value as  the maximum number of cores that can be used to spawn new jobs. If set to a value less than 0, then the spawn server will use all available cores on the node that are not used by the main application. Default: 0
